cblink carries netlink-style messages between userland programs: a
fixed binary header followed by a CBOR body of typed attributes.
Servers register families of operations with declarative attribute
policies; clients resolve families by name and use request/response,
dumps, flow-controlled streams and multicast notifications.

It runs over TCP with TLS 1.3, SCTP with DTLS 1.2, and local
sockets, with mutual TLS by default.

cblink-gen generates typed C code and documentation from a family's
YAML spec, much like YNL does for Linux netlink.
